  "findings": [
    "An idle civilian salvor cone accelerated 22 asteroid and 4 ship lives in the 20-second baseline. The final salvor field acts on one payload and no asteroid or ship.",
    "Unattributed origin=choir_relief preset subsystem injuries at sim0 raised an unwarranted civilian violence alarm. Final classification retains the damage/medical state but suppresses that false alarm.",
    "A genuine escape now turns toward its escape direction before full thrust/boost and brakes inward motion while turning; dedicated worker tests cover that situation.",
    "After those first corrections, a 140-WU ambient orbit with 0.7 rad/s angular motion still superseded the miner job. The intermediate capture revealed 127.237 WU/s and hull damage. Final errand ownership preserves authored work and uses bounded physical guidance for generic idle loops.",
    "Final opening has no ship/wreck kill events and no asteroid fractures. All three focus hulls survive intact. Minor late worker contact consumes shields and raises a brief real-contact alarm; collision-free traffic is not claimed."
  ],
